with millions of credit card purchases  daily detecting fraudulent transactions  before they can complete is more  important than ever I'm Billy Jacobson a  developer Advocate with a focus on cloud  databases and in this video we'll look  at how we can use big data processing  tools machine learning endpoints and the  low latency and highly scalable bigtable  database to detect fraud in milliseconds  thank you  [Music]  when a customer initiates a credit card  purchase the transaction is sent for  processing before the purchase can be  completed the system needs to validate  the credit card check for fraud and then  add it to the customer's transaction  history once the result is in the  transaction can be completed if no fraud  was detected otherwise the customer  might receive a fraud alert and can  block any further transactions until  their account can be secured all of  these actions are happening during a  customer's checkout flow so we need to  ensure low latency processing to provide  a smooth experience for millions of  shoppers  let's look at how we can create a  scalable system that supports this use  case the first step towards detecting  fraud is managing the stream of customer  transactions we need an event streaming  service that can horizontally scale to  meet the workload traffic so Cloud Pub  sub is a great choice I can simulate a  transaction by sending a pub sub message  with the user ID timestamp transaction  ID price merchant ID Merchant  geolocation and then a question mark to  indicate the fraud status in real life  we just do this programmatically using  the client libraries Pub sub has a  built-in integration with Google Cloud's  data pipeline tool Cloud dataflow let's  look at my transaction pipeline in the  dataflow UI this will allow us to  process the stream of transactions at  scale  to determine if a transaction is fraud  we'll compare the pending transaction  with the customer's historical  transaction patterns and their user  profile  we're using bigtable as a feature store  here with column families or customer  transaction history and user profile  bigtable is highly scalable and has  consistent single digit millisecond  latency so there's less time used for  fetching data and more time available  for processing data  before we developed our pipeline we used  machine learning to train a fraud  detection model based on our transaction  history and then use vertex AI endpoints  to deploy the model to a managed service  vertex AI supports custom models  developed on any framework and has  built-in tooling to track our model's  performance  now with our Pipeline and model deployed  we'll send our pending transaction  historical data and user profile to the  model and receive our prediction back  which we've outputted to the worker logs  the fraud probability on this one is low  awesome we can let the transaction  complete  with this prediction in hand we send it  to a pub sub output stream the credit  card processing can complete if no fraud  was detected or we could send a push  notification to let the customer know  there is a fraud attempt on their  account  we also can write the new transaction to  bigtable so it can be used as a data  point for future transactions bigtable  scales horizontally for reading and  writing data so keeping our feature  store up to date is as easy as querying  it this is a simplified example of a  fraud detection system we use tools with  horizontal scalability to ensure our  system is prepared for when we go from  thousands of customers to Millions  during a big event and we have a low  latency database keeping our checkout  flow running smoothly at any scale  if you're interested in deploying this  solution yourself you can find links to  the code source with a terraform setup  in the description we'll link to more  resources on Raw detection for you to  read further thanks for watching  [Music]
 

